+## Key Design Decisions
+
+### Preserve concurrent edits as whole-visit revisions
+
+Each submitted edit is retained as a complete visit revision. When independent corrections are based on the same earlier revision, the record store sends the competing revisions to review rather than combining their fields automatically. A visit with unresolved competing revisions cannot enter the reviewed CSV export.
+
+Field-aware three-way merge remains a credible alternative because it could combine non-overlapping changes automatically and reduce the review queue. It would require tablets to retain base snapshots and submit structured field changes, and it would require the record store to maintain field-level provenance and merge rules. The team has chosen whole-visit revisions because independently edited fields can still be scientifically related; automatically combining them could create an observation that no field worker actually made and whose meaning is difficult to review.
+
+Tablet sync must retain the base revision identifier for each edit and present a submission outcome that distinguishes an accepted current revision from a revision awaiting review. Review and export must show the competing complete revisions for a visit, let coordinators select the revision that becomes current, and exclude unresolved visits from CSV generation.
